---
import { DATA_ATTRIBUTIONS } from "@gof/shared/places";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { correctionsEmail } from "../lib/contact.ts";

export const prerender = true;
const email = correctionsEmail();
---

<Base
  title="About Golf Outing Finder"
  description="How Golf Outing Finder lists golf outings anyone can pay to enter, how listings are checked, and where our course and map data comes from."
  path="/about"
  crumbs={[{ name: "About", path: "/about" }]}
>
  <h1>About Golf Outing Finder</h1>
  <p>
    Golf Outing Finder lists golf outings in the United States that anyone can pay to enter: charity scrambles, school
    fundraisers, trade group days, open tournaments and access days, at municipal, public, semi-private, private and resort
    courses. A $125 muni scramble gets the same listing as a charity day at a private club.
  </p>
  <h2>How listings get here</h2>
  <p>
    Every night a program looks for outings on organizers' websites and registration platforms, reads the date, course, price
    and what's included, and matches the outing to a course. When it isn't sure, it holds the listing back instead of
    publishing it. Each listing links to its source and shows when we last checked it.
  </p>
  <p>
    We write every summary in our own words and never copy organizers' text, images or logos. When a listing says "Charity",
    we've matched the organizer to IRS records of 501(c)(3) organizations. Other fundraisers say their charity status is
    unverified.
  </p>
  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>The site is free to use. It may show display ads. Organizers never pay to be listed, and we don't handle registration or payments.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and removals</h2>
  <p>
    Organizers can ask us to fix or remove a listing at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. See
    <a href="/corrections">corrections</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Data sources and credits</h2>
  <ul>
    {
      DATA_ATTRIBUTIONS.map((a) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{a.name}</strong>: {a.text} <a href={a.url}>{a.url.replace(/^https:\/\//, "")}</a> ({a.license})
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
</Base>
